Angular Reactive Forms:
 ->> To build complex and dynamic forms
 ->> Reactive forms allow to create form objects and link them to forms, to which- we can further add validation. 
 ->> Reactive forms module is used for handling and providing various ways to manage the form controls, their values and validation.

Form Group:
 ->> Form Group is a class that is used for wrapping a collection of Form Controls.
 ->> A Form Control within a form Group represents an individual form control to manage the state, value and validation.

Form Array:
 ->> A Form Array is a class which represents a collection or an array of form controls, form groups or form arrays.
 ->> It is very useful to handle dynamic sets of form control and perform validations on them.

   FormGroup <--- FormArray <--- FormControl

FormBuilder
 ->> FormBuilder class simplifies the process of building and handling forms within the application.
 ->> This reduces boiler plate code and makes form creation process more concise and readable.

Validating form controls:
 ->> It check for the fields touched or not e.g nameControl, emailControl

 
dirty property and pristine property: used to control and manage the form states.
                                      useful in tracking the form control state.
                                      privide essential information about the user interaction.
                                      Return boolean value.

Dirty property: becomes true when the user interacts with the control and modifies its value.(touched and altered by the user)
                Default : false

pristine property: it indicates the control is in its original state i.e unchaged state.Stays true until user interacted.
                   Default : true